    <!-- SEO PROSE 3: HOW THIS LIST WAS COMPILED -->
    <section class="mb-14">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-4">How this list was compiled</h2>
      <div class="prose-custom max-w-none text-sm text-stone-700 space-y-4">
        <p>Every entry was researched independently from each agency's own website, LinkedIn profile, and, for the largest firms, public financial disclosures. No agency paid for inclusion or for placement on this list. The shortlist deliberately includes both dedicated AI agencies and the AI practices of larger, established consulting and engineering firms, since both categories compete for the same buyer decision in practice.</p>
        <p>The editorial criteria applied were advisory independence (evidence of recommending against a project, not just for one), named enterprise engagements, documented methodology, strategy-to-build continuity, and engagement transparency. Agencies with no verifiable AI advisory track record, or whose "consulting" offering turned out to be a thin wrapper around a fixed build package, were excluded regardless of brand size.</p>
        <p>Ratings are editorial and specific to suitability as an AI consulting agency on this list, not an aggregate of third-party review scores and not a measure of general company quality. Team size and reported headcount figures are drawn from LinkedIn and each firm's own disclosures and can vary across public sources for large multinationals; verify current figures directly with each agency before a procurement decision.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- FAQ -->
    <section class="mb-14">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-8">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="space-y-6">
        <div class="border-b border-stone-100 pb-6">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-2">What does an AI consulting agency actually deliver?</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-stone-600">A prioritized, tested set of recommendations for where AI can return more than it costs, usually including a readiness assessment of your data and systems, a shortlist of viable use cases, and either a technical roadmap or a working pilot. It is not the same engagement as hiring a development team to build a specific application from a spec you already have.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="border-b border-stone-100 pb-6">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-2">How much does AI consulting cost?</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-stone-600">A standalone strategy or readiness assessment typically runs $15K to $60K over three to eight weeks. Ongoing advisory work runs $8K to $30K per month on retainer. Agencies that hand off directly into a dedicated build team charge separately for that phase, usually $10K to $25K per engineer per month.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="border-b border-stone-100 pb-6">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-2">How do I build a shortlist of AI consulting agencies?</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-stone-600">Start with three to five agencies, not fifteen. Filter on advisory independence, a documented and repeatable methodology, named enterprise engagements you can verify, and a clear plan for how strategy work connects to implementation. See the comparison table above for how each agency on this list scores against those criteria.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="border-b border-stone-100 pb-6">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-2">Is a Big Four or global agency better than a boutique AI consulting agency?</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-stone-600">Neither is categorically better. Large agencies bring scale, existing enterprise relationships, and dedicated technical arms with real engineering depth. Boutique agencies tend to move faster, cost less, and, if they have no separate implementation business to protect, can give more candid advice about whether a project is worth doing at all.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pb-6">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-2">What is the best AI consulting agency for a startup budget?</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-stone-600">Smaller, founder-led agencies with team sizes under 50 tend to price strategy engagements for startup budgets rather than enterprise ones. Check the minimum engagement table above; agencies like SoftKraft and DataRoot Labs are built specifically for startup-stage clients rather than Fortune 500 procurement cycles.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

